course: dictionary
lesson: 4141
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the words around them. Read the context first, then decide which meaning fits. «It was simply glorious!» The sentence does not say what was glorious, but the feeling is happy and excited, so glorious means wonderful and enjoyable here.
explain: The same word can mean different things. A glorious sunset is very beautiful to look at, a glorious day is bright, sunny and warm, and a glorious victory is one that brings great fame and honour. Ask yourself what is being described, then pick the meaning that suits it.
explain: Toad says, «Glorious, stirring sight!» A stirring sight is one that moves you deeply, so glorious shows that Toad is amazed and full of admiration. To check your meaning, swap in a word like wonderful. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Glorious is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in a glorious day or a glorious sunset.
fact: Its forms are glorious, more glorious and most glorious.
fact: «Glorious» can mean very beautiful and wonderful to see or feel.
fact: In weather talk, «glorious» means bright, sunny and warm, as in «glorious sunshine».
fact: In history and poetry, «glorious victory» means a win that brings great fame, honour and praise.
exercise: «It was simply glorious!» What does glorious mean here? | Lost in the woods | *Wonderful and enjoyable | Cold and wet | Very quiet
exercise: The team's glorious victory made the whole town proud. What does glorious mean here? | *Brought great fame and honour | Was very quiet and calm | Lost badly and felt sad | Was raining hard
exercise: Toad says, «Glorious, stirring sight!» What does stirring suggest? | Boring and dull | Noisy and rude | *Moving you deeply and filling you with feeling | Sleepy and quiet
test: A glorious sunset is one that is | *Very beautiful and wonderful to see | Cloudy and grey | Very small and quiet
test: What does glorious mean in «glorious sunshine»? | *Bright, sunny and warm | Very loud | Frozen and icy | Old and broken
exam: Which sentence uses glorious to mean very enjoyable? | The glorious king lost the battle. | The glorious mountain was covered in snow. | *We had a glorious time at the party. | The glorious rain fell all night.
